Found while running the author tests for karr #159; pre-existing at 42f15b8 and
NOT caused by that change. Filed rather than acted on.

    prove -lr xt/
    xt/author/pod-links.t (Wstat: 2560) Tests: 11 Failed: 10
    Failed tests: 1-9, 11

Every failure is the same two things, in every module:

  *** ERROR: Unknown directive: =method at line 689 in file lib/File/SOPS.pm
  *** ERROR: unresolved internal link 'rotate' at line 180 in file ...

`=method` is Pod::Weaver's, supplied by [@Author::GETTY] at build time, so
Pod::Checker reading the SOURCE sees an unknown directive and then cannot
resolve any L</method> link that points at one. The test therefore fails on
every file that uses the house POD conventions -- which is all of them -- and
has presumably been failing since those conventions landed.

One extra, real and separate: lib/File/SOPS.pm line 241 has a non-ASCII
character (a literal cafe-with-accent in `C<caf...>`) before any `=encoding`
directive.

Two ways out, both cheap:
  * run the check against the BUILT distribution (dzil build, then check
    blib/) where Pod::Weaver has already turned =method into =head2; or
  * teach the test the custom directives before parsing.

Either way an author test that fails at every commit is one nobody reads, and it
is the file that would catch a genuinely broken POD link. Lane: whoever owns the
release checks; the =encoding line is api's file.

Verified: prove -lr xt/ reproduced the failure exactly as described (10/11 subtests failed, 'Unknown directive: =method' + unresolved internal link errors on raw lib/). Confirmed the =method/=attr/... directives are Pod::Weaver's from [@Author::GETTY] (getty-perl-release-author-getty skill), unknown to Pod::Checker before weaving.

Fix (xt/author/pod-links.t only): detect whether we're checking the raw source tree (.git present -- Git::GatherDir never copies .git into a dzil build, so this is the same signal the original design already reasoned about) vs an already-woven copy (dzil test's own promoted t/author-pod-links.t, .git absent). In the raw case, run 'dzil build --in $tempdir' to weave the POD into a throwaway copy first, then podcheck THAT; in the already-woven case, behavior is unchanged from before. Did NOT take the 'teach podchecker the directives' route -- that would silence the unknown-directive error but leave every L</method_name> unresolved (still noise, still blind to a real dead link).

Proof the net still catches a real break: copied the whole repo (incl. .git) to a scratch dir, mutated one valid L</rotate> link in lib/File/SOPS.pm to L</rotate_this_target_does_not_exist>, ran 'prove -lv xt/author/pod-links.t' from that copy -- test 1 (SOPS.pm) failed with the exact broken target named in the diagnostic, the other 10 files still passed. Net can still fall.

Confirmed out of scope, untouched: the ~17 external L<...|https://...> docs/adr/* links (karr #126) -- Pod::Checker never resolves scheme'd URLs, so they were already silent (0 errors) on the full woven build before my change and remain so; no special-casing needed or added.

